WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.730
If you want to hear how one forgotten scene
from the book makes a little easter egg appearance

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.180
in this movie then stick around to the end
of this video.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.180
This video is sponsored by Raycon.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.440
[Intro]

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.530
Welcome to Things You Missed, today we continue
the Carriethon...

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.599
Yeah, I'm calling it that now, with yet another
remake of Carrie, but this one, while not

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:21.909
as subliminal as the original, is actually
pretty good.

00:00:21.909 --> 00:00:24.279
It makes some improvements and has some of
its own secrets.

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.399
So why don't we explore them?

00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:29.359
[Things You Missed]

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:32.320
The volleyball game from the novel has been
changed to pool volleyball for the remake.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.640
I think it makes a lot of sense, because of
the maturity of the female body is a major

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.350
theme in Carrie, and the swimsuits are just going
to highlight that.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.600
Also, putting them in a pool gives more of
a reason for the shower scene to exist in

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.160
order to wash off that chlorine, since in this
time period, most kids would just slap on

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.290
some deodorant after a regular gym class.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.650
Ms. Desjardin, basically looked like
Misty from Pokèmon in this scene.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.260
Misty is a water type trainer and the gym
leader of the Cerulean City gym, while Ms.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.400
D trains her students in water, and is the
gym teacher of the Ewen High School Gym.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.650
Misty is known for nurturing the awkward,
misunderstood Psyduck, and Ms. D forms a special

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.059
bond with Carrie White.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:07.670
When Carrie gets her first period in the shower
after class, I noticed this sign in the locker

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.539
room, which could foreshadow something that
happens in the prom scene where the twins

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:12.020
slip and fall on the wet floor.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.369
I think there's a similar foreshadowing going
on with these umbrellas in Sue Snell's house

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:19.329
to setup the sprinklers at prom and when Carrie
uses her mind to break the locker room mirror

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.170
which sets up this part and this part.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:24.810
Lately, we've seen a number a Stephen King's
novels get adapted for a second time, like

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:28.210
Pet Sematary and IT, but this movie seems
to want us to know that's it's just as much

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.790
of a remake of Brian DePalma's 1976 film than
it is a re-adaptation of the novel.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.030
The car that Billy Nolan drives looks the
same, the theme of the prom seems to once

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.640
again be "Love Among The Stars" as opposed
to "Springtime in Venice" from the novel,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.000
Carrie's dress is pink (or at least it starts
out that way), Carrie’s mother is crucified,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.020
and Sue Snell's nightmare at the end is re-imagined,
and this isn't something that's in the book at all.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.359
Carrie after recording Carrie's meltdown in
the locker room, Chris Hargensen, who is so

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:53.149
narcissistic that she has a picture of herself,
uploads it to YouTube.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:57.009
it actually kind of giving me anxiety that
the tags and description aren't properly filled

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:58.009
out.

00:01:58.009 --> 00:02:00.909
The girls who bullied Carrie are forced to
run sprints, but the rules are a bit different

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:02.180
than in the original.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.560
"That's up to all of you but anyone who stops running

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.679
is suspended.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.600
And if you're suspended, you're not going to prom."

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.750
I kind of feel like that's not that effective,
because the girls who most guilty are pretty

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.140
fit, so continuing to run wouldn't really be that
big of a deal for them compared to the others.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.950
Anyway, while this is going on, Carrie is
excused from gym, and picks up some books

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.600
from the library, one of which is called Telekinesis:
Analysis and Aftermath.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.360
In the novel, the story is broken up by excerpts
from books, articles and interviews about

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.700
the Carrie White incident and about the telekinesis
phenomenon, and this is one of the many publications

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.700
quoted.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.390
The poem Carrie reads from in English class
is an excerpt from John Milton's 1671 poem

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.980
"Samson Agonistes".

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.160
I think that's how you say it.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:46.020
It too hints at the tragic ending of this
story with lines like “From restless thoughts,

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.650
that like a deadly swarm of hornets arm’d,”
which connects to the idea of Carrie’s thoughts

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.840
literally being deadly because she can destroy
things with her mind and “of both my Parents

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.070
all in flames ascended,” which ties into
her mother’s idea that Carrie was born out

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.560
of sin and of course the fiery ending of the
senior prom.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.280
One of the things I mentioned at the beginning
is how there are some little improvements

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.980
in certain areas, like how we're really shown
the weight of Sue's decision to miss the prom

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:10.110
in this one -- the fact that she's been dreaming
of it since she was young, how she already

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.760
has a dress picked out and how everyone expects
her to be there.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.570
There are also some creative uses of the Telekinesis,
like how Carrie uses it to flip the light

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.800
switch moments before her mother walks in,
using it to hold down the foot pedal on the

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.840
sewing machine without actually using her
foot, and perhaps the most lazy one I've ever

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.260
seen, using it to turn on the radio.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.600
It's right there, Carrie.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.930
It's literally right there.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.990
So Sue asks her boyfriend Tommy Ross to take
Carrie to the prom.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:34.990
As always.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.810
But this time, rather than Tommy being a baseball
player, football phenom or track star, he

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:41.860
keeps up with the theme of this being set
in 2013 and plays LaCrosse.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.100
Should have gone with ultimate.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.680
However, Carrie's mother does not approve
of her attending the prom.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.760
Let’s roll it.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.040
“They’ll paw at you.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.620
They find where that blood smell comes from.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.960
He’s gonna take you, Carrie, in his car
out into the wilderness.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.580
Out where it’s cold and where the roadhouses
are and the whiskey.”

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.100
In the novel, roadhouses and whiskey are one
of those things that come up again and again

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.400
as a symbol of evil in the eyes of Mrs. White.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.180
For example, her father was killed in roadhouse,
her husband impregnated her with the smell

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.810
of roadhouse whiskey on his breath and at
the end of the book Carrie chases Chris Hargensen

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.319
and Billy Nolan to a roadhouse called the
Cavalier, which by the way is represented

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:15.720
by an easter egg in the movie.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.750
"A bunch of people were going to the Cavalier
after".

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:21.290
The Cavalier is where Chris and Billy sleep
sometimes and where they devise the plan to

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.350
humiliate Carrie.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.220
The movie also shows step one of that plan
going into action when Billy and his friends

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.220
go to the pig farm.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.560
"Don't worry little piggy.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.860
Uncle Jack is gonna bash your head right
in.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.920
They just really couldn’t help themselves
in this franchise could they?

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:39.610
“I’m just gonna bash your brains in. I'm gonna bash em right the heck in!”

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.990
The day of the prom would soon arrive.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.290
Carrie and Tommy hang with Tommy’s friend
George and his date Erika, who goes to a different

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.290
school called Dover.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.740
It actually works well that she is from another
school because she has no reason to think

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.850
Carrie is weird at all.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.440
That was me at prom.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.610
The kid… from another school.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.850
But if you ask me, Sue Snell is the real weird
one in this movie, her boyfriend is literally

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.810
the only conversation in her phone.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.720
This, supposed Prom Queen favorite seriously
only talks to one person?

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.720
Come on.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.770
If you pause the movie as the students are
filling out their votes for Prom King and

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:10.940
Queen, there are even more easter eggs and
other Things You Missed.

