00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:21.400
There's a lot more than what meets the eye on the prom King and Queen ballot.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.540
First we got Frank Grier and Jessica Upshaw.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.640
Frank was a football player in the book and
Jessica Upshaw is one of the bullies.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.370
George Chizmar and Frieda Jason.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.370
George was the most renowned artist at the
school who created murals displayed at the

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.520
prom and Frieda is his girlfriend.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.520
These write ins are a joke, Morton and Desjardin.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.480
Morton if you don’t remember is the assistant
principal, and Desjardin is the gym teacher,

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.449
so I imagine this ballot was filled by one
of the girls who was punished for bullying

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:45.490
Carrie White and still upset about Morton
and Desjardin teaming up to dish out the punishment.

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.000
Don Farnham and Helen Shyres.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.460
Don’s only mention in the book is that he’s
dating Helen and Helen is another one of the

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.460
bullies.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.880
After Tommy Ross and Carrie White, we’ve
got Brian Cranstone and Emma Tamblyn.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.760
Brian, not to be confused with the dad from
Malcolm in the Middle is gets his name from

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.220
the on set carpenter of Carrie (he also worked
on It and It Chapter 2) and Emma worked the

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.220
in the costume department.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:07.190
Not sure about Peter Nicolakakos, but Myra
Crewes is a minor character in the novel.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.919
And finally: Jordan Samuel and Susan Reilly
Lehane.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.420
Jordan was the head of the makeup department
and Susan was the makeup artist for Juliane

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.080
Moore.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.240
This one might be the coolest looking blood
spill, although I don’t know if I can show

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.070
it, Carrie force chokes Ms Desjardin… hopefully
I can show that, and after destroying the

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:22.889
prom, returns home to face her mother.

00:07:22.889 --> 00:07:26.030
Margret White’s only real hobby seems to
be sewing, so I found it kind of cool that

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:29.760
Carrie uses that against her by impaling her
with all her own tools.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.360
Wait, where have I seen this before?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:36.080
"Look at this! I took 9 million steps today!"

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.950
There’s nothing more terrifying than that.

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.940
Finally, Carrie uses her telekinesis to bring
down the entire house, but there’s

00:07:40.949 --> 00:07:43.880
one small moment where we see what is actually
destroying it.

00:07:43.889 --> 00:07:46.949
After lifting up her mother, a rock can be
seen punching through the ceiling and landing

00:07:46.949 --> 00:07:47.949
on this dresser.

00:07:47.949 --> 00:07:51.420
This is a reference to an event from the book
known as the Rain of Stones, which is documented

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:55.110
in a weekly magazine that tells of an incident
that took place when Carrie was a little girl.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:58.699
Accounts from the Whites’ neighbors say
one day after Margret upset her, rocks started

00:07:58.699 --> 00:08:02.919
to fall from the sky, but only above the White's
house, and pierce through the roof tiles while

00:08:02.919 --> 00:08:04.139
Carrie was having a meltdown.

00:08:04.139 --> 00:08:07.550
However, the story never really became mainstream
because by the time the media showed up, Mrs.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.050
White had already had the roof repaired, but
all the neighbors swear by what happened.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.759
The scene has only been adapted in the 2002
TV movie, where the stones look more like

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:15.759
meteors.

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:19.610
Apparently it was planned to be included in
both theatrical movies, but got cut both times,

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:20.850
other than this little easter egg.

